                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "TL:DR:\nBad optimization, soggy controls and response time, mediocre graphics, full of bugs, questionable hit detection, low server populations, and an overall terrible clone of KotK/PUBG.  Even for early access, this is a stinker.  Not worth $5 currently.\n\nFirst Impression Gameplay:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8wUagD3n4U0\n\nOh man, where to start with this one?  Well to start off, the game wouldn’t properly start.  Stuck at 1fps after launching.  A restart resolved the issue but introduced another issue: no sound once entering the lobby.  Third time was the charm and I loaded up without any more serious bugs.\n\nMinor bugs can be found all over the place, including the need to jump at the top of stairs, ghost weapons stuck on your players back, random dying after being shot seconds prior, items all spawning in a giant heap, ect.\n\nOnce in the game, it became painfully obvious how much this game ripped off PUBG/KotK: \n1. The main menu screen is almost the same as PUBG\n2. You spawn in a staging area with a countdown to start\n3. Begin in a cargo plane and parachute to the ground\n4. Enter houses and pick up familiar items such as bandages, energy drinks, and all the familiar PUBG/H1Z1 weapons\n5. Equip backpacks and motorcycle helmets\n6. Encroaching death zone\n\nI could keep going on, but its basically an uninspired rip-off executed poorly.  \nSounds feel dull and low quality, graphics are muddy, and controls are just god awful.\nWhy do you need to hold in left click to fire the shotgun?  Very clunky.\n\nHit detection and damage delegation is questionable, as I shot a guy server times from the bottom of some stairs and he didn’t die.  Blood splattered each time, so I’m not sure what’s going on there.  I was killed within a few shots.  I also got run over by a jeep that was about 10 feet away on my screen.  Really, just watch my first impression video if you don't believe me.\n\nOverall, I think this is a prime example of why developers need to bug test and not take advantage of early access if the game isn’t in a playable state.  They would be much better off leaving this free for now and letting people play who are aware that they are doing early stage bug testing.\n",
